adjudication.rationale:
In `emailReminderManager.ts`, `deleteScheduledEmailReminder(reminderId, referenceId, immediateDelete)` returns early when `immediateDelete` is true after canceling the SendGrid batch, without updating `WorkflowReminder.cancelled` or deleting the row:
```ts
if (immediateDelete) {
  await client.request({ ... status: "cancel" ... });
  return;
}
```
Call sites in the diff pass `true` (e.g. `handleNewBooking.ts` reschedule and several paths in `workflows.tsx`), and the previous explicit Prisma `deleteMany` logic was removed in those places. The new cleanup in `scheduleEmailReminders.ts` only targets `cancelled: true`, so these rows are not picked up for deletion, matching the finding’s “orphaned DB row” concern.
